      "s": "동아일보",
      "t": "케어랩스, 사명 ‘원익H&X’로 변경",
      "d": "케어랩스가 사명을 ‘원익H&X’로 변경하고, 생애 맞춤형 웰니스 기업으로 새롭게 도약한다고 26일 밝혔다. 회사는 이날 임시주주총회를 열고, 사명 변경을 위한 정관 일부 변경의 건을 원안대로 의결했다. 이번 사명 변경은 반도체 장비 기업인 원익그룹 계열사로서 정체성을 강화하는 동시에, 생애 단계에 맞춘 헬스·뷰티·시니어 케어 경험을 제공하겠다는 회사의 방향성을 반영하기 위해 추진됐다. 새 사명 ‘원익H&X’에서 ‘H’는 사람(Human)과 건강(Health), 헬스케어(Healthcare)를 뜻하며, ‘X’는 확장(eXpansion)과 경험(eXperience), 전환(X, Transformation)을 상징한다.",
      "u": "https://www.donga.com/news/Economy/article/all/20261126/135098682/2",
      "m": "11. 26. PM 03:30",
      "ts": 1795707000000,
      "fullText": "최지원 기자 구독"
    },
    {
      "s": "Bloomberg Tech",
      "t": "Netherlands to Fight Rollout of Proposed US Curbs on ASML",
      "d": "The Dutch government said it will resist US plans to further restrict ASML Holding NV’s sales to China, calling the proposed rules a threat to Europe’s most valuable company and widening a rift with Washington.",
      "u": "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-26/netherlands-plans-to-fight-rollout-of-proposed-us-curbs-on-asml",
      "m": "11. 26. PM 12:23",
      "ts": 1795695792000,
      "fullText": "Technology Netherlands to Fight Rollout of Proposed US Curbs on ASML Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift Gift this article Contact us: Provide news feedback or report an error Confidential tip? Send a tip to our reporters Site feedback: Take our Survey New Window Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift By Patrick Van Oosterom and Sarah Jacob November 26, 2026 at 12:23 PM UTC Updated on November 26, 2026 at 2:59 PM UTC Bookmark Save Takeaways by Bloomberg AI The Dutch government said it will resist US plans to further restrict ASML Holding NV ’s sales to China, calling the proposed rules a threat to Europe’s most valuable company and widening a rift with Washington. The US’s Match Act, which aims to stymie China’s progress in the chip industry, would force the Netherlands and other allies to strengthen export controls on advanced equipment, including Veldhoven, Netherlands-based ASML’s chipmaking machines. The Dutch government is opposed to the extraterritorial scope of the bill, trade minister Sjoerd Sjoerdsma said in parliament on Thursday."
    },
